 *footclient claude* is resumed rather than restarted.
 
+# SECTION: session-duplicate
+
+Rules used by *Duplicate* in a tab's context menu, with the same
+syntax and expansion as *session-restore*. They are evaluated when
+the tab is duplicated (for at most two seconds), and the new tab
+re-runs the resulting programs without the saved screen content.
+Programs without a rule here fall back to their *session-restore*
+rule.
+
+Example:
+
+```
+[session-duplicate]
+claude=claude --resume "$(jq -r .sessionId "${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}/sessions/$FOOT_PID.json")" --fork-session
+```
+
+# SECTION: tabs
+
+Several terminals (tabs) can share one window. Every window has a
+sidebar listing its tabs. Session restore brings each window back
+with all its tabs, split views and sidebar state.
+
+Sidebar mouse actions: left-click a tab to select it;
+*Control*-click or *Shift*-click to select several (right-click a
+selected tab to split or close them together); drag a tab to reorder
+it, onto a terminal to show it side by side with that window's
+current tab, onto another foot window's sidebar to move it there, or
+anywhere else to detach it into its own window; middle-click to close
+it; right-click for a menu (close, kill, duplicate, split, unsplit)
+driven by mouse or *Up*/*Down*/*Return*/*Escape*. Drag the sidebar's
+inner edge to resize it. The bottom row has *+* for a new tab and an
+arrow that hides the sidebar; a hidden sidebar leaves an arrow in the
+bottom corner that shows it again.
+
+In a split view, the first click on an unfocused pane only focuses
+it.
+
+Each tab's shell gets *FOOT_TAB_ID*; *footclient --focus-tab* brings
+that tab to the front, e.g. from a notification action.
+
+*Kill* sends SIGKILL to the tab's foreground process group and its
+shell, after a confirmation. *Close* hangs up as when closing a
+window. *Duplicate* opens a new tab running what the tab runs, see
+*session-duplicate*.
+
+*width*
+	Default sidebar width, in pixels (scaled). Default: _200_.
+
+*show*
+	Boolean. Whether new windows show the sidebar. Default: _no_.
+
+*position*
+	Sidebar side: _left_ or _right_. Default: _left_.
+
+*activity*
+	Boolean. Mark background tabs that print new lines. Redraws in
+	place, such as spinners and status lines, don't count. Default:
+	_yes_.
